{
  "slug": "ballot-problem-oq-05-oq-02",
  "title": "The Reflection-Principle Form of the Ballot Number, BN(a,b) = C(a+b,b) − C(a+b,b−1)",
  "phase": "OBSERVE",
  "status": "available",
  "tier": "B",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\mathrm{BN}(a,b) = \\binom{a+b}{b} - \\binom{a+b}{b-1} \\quad (a \\ge 1), \\text{ equivalently } \\binom{a+b-1}{a-1} - \\binom{a+b-1}{a} = \\binom{a+b}{b} - \\binom{a+b}{b-1}.",
    "plain": "The ballot number BN(a,b) counts sequences of a up-steps and b down-steps whose every partial sum stays strictly positive. The parent entry defines it as C(a+b-1,a-1) - C(a+b-1,a); this problem proves the alternative reflection-principle form C(a+b,b) - C(a+b,b-1) (André's derivation) and reconciles the two derivations of the ballot number in a single Lean file.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "The ballot number has two famous elementary derivations — the Dvoretzky–Motzkin cycle lemma and André's reflection principle — that produce different-looking closed forms; reconciling them is exactly showing the two derivations agree.",
      "Formalizing the equality turns combinatorial folklore into a machine-checked binomial identity and completes the arithmetic layer of the ballot family alongside the parent's probability and Catalan corollaries.",
      "It exercises the pure binomial-shift API (Pascal's rule and symmetry C(n,k) = C(n,n-k)) that recurs throughout the ballot/Catalan strand."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [],
    "open": [
      "The equality C(a+b-1,a-1) - C(a+b-1,a) = C(a+b,b) - C(a+b,b-1) has not been formalized in this repository.",
      "The reflection-principle derivation and the cycle-lemma derivation of the ballot number have not been reconciled in a single Lean file."
    ],
    "goal": "Prove ballotNumber a b = C(a+b,b) - C(a+b,b-1) for a ≥ 1 (as a truncated natural-number identity), reusing the parent's ballotNumber definition, and assemble the reflection form together with the existing cycle-lemma/aggregate results so both derivations of BN(a,b) live in one file."
  },
